    "text_full": "Cookie Settings\nMain Content\nMain Menu\nSEARCH\nMENU\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nInclusion and Engagement\nInclusion and Engagement\n\nInclusion and engagement are core pillars of our firm.\nWe attribute our success to the diversity of our firm\n– our people, our practices, our clients. \n\nTo learn more, visit the pages below. \n\nON THIS PAGE:\nOverview\nAwards\nInclusion Report\nInclusion and Engagement Committee\nAffinity Groups\nPipeline Initiatives\n\nOVERVIEW\n\nMessage from the Chief Inclusion and Engagement Officer\n\nAt Wiley, we aim to leverage our collaborative culture to celebrate the collective strength of all people – all under one umbrella. It is our recipe for success. This success is realized one person at a time. Each moment and interaction that we have – when we do it right, creates a firm where all the best talent belongs. Our investments in sustaining an inclusive work environment enable us to deliver best-in-class legal services. \n\n- Rashida MacMurray-Abdullah\n\n\tInclusion and Engagement Statement: Please click here to read the firm’s Inclusion and Engagement Statement.\nAwards\nBest Law Firms for Talent, Seramount 2025 \nEquality 100 Award, Human Rights Campaign Foundation (HRCF) 2025 \nRanked #13 of Largest Law Firms in Greater Washington, Washington Business Journal 2025 \n\nDiversity, Equity, and Inclusion Framework, Bloomberg Law 2024\nDiversity, Equity, & Inclusion – The Elite, Chambers Associate 2024\nCompass Award, Leadership Council on Legal Diversity 2024\nTop Performer, Leadership Council on Legal Diversity 2024\nBest Law Firm for Women & Diversity, Seramount 2024\nBest Companies to Work For: Law Firms, U.S. News & World Report 2024\nMost Influential Lawyers, Savoy Magazine 2024 ( Powell-Woodson and D. Holland)\nRashida MacMurray-Abdullah\nCHIEF INCLUSION AND ENGAGEMENT OFFICER\nrmacmurray-abdullah@wiley.law\n202.719.3305\n\n2024 INCLUSION REPORT\nInclusion in Action\n\nIn 2024, we made meaningful progress in fostering a culture of inclusion by investing in the growth and well-being of our people, clients, and community. This annual report highlights a few of the impactful initiatives that have shaped our firm and strengthened our engagement with the Washington, DC area.\n\nView the report\n\n\nHOW DOES WILEY WORK TO FOSTER INCLUSION AND BELONGING ACROSS THE FIRM?\n\n\"At Wiley, we are committed to fostering a culture of belonging. We take pride in our diversity of thought, identity, and lived experiences. A fair and inclusive workplace makes us stronger and helps us work together to produce the best results.\"\n\n\n\nDuane C. Pozza, Inclusion and Engagement Committee Chair \n\nAFFINITY GROUPS\nBringing people together\nMeet the leaders\nPIPELINE INITIATIVES\nEngaging the community\nLearn more\nPeople\nPractices\nInsights\nFirm\nCareers\nInclusion and Engagement\nHome\nSite Map\nTerms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nCookies Policy & Settings\nCalifornia Privacy Notice\n© 2026 Wiley Rein LLP All Rights Reserved.\nSubscribe\n\nOur Site uses cookies to improve your experience. Cookies may collect your personal information, such as IP address or device identifier, which we may disclose to our analytics partners. You may opt out of the cookies that are not strictly necessary if you wish. By using this site, you agree to our updated Privacy Policy, Terms & Conditions, and Cookies Policy.\n\nCUSTOMIZE COOKIE CHOICES\nREJECT ALL COOKIES\nACCEPT ALL COOKIES"
